The attached image (Figure 4) illustrates the uptake of FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) and AF647-labeled Nano-11 by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) via confocal microscopy. The top row shows BMDCs incubated with Nano-11 (red), indicating its cellular uptake. The middle row shows minimal uptake of soluble OVA (green). The bottom row demonstrates significantly enhanced intracellular delivery of OVA when adsorbed to Nano-11, with widespread co-localization of OVA and Nano-11 within the cells, suggesting that Nano-11 acts as an efficient delivery vehicle for antigens to dendritic cells.